{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek","id":381572,"title":"Thought Experiment: Hypothetical Exigent of Lytek","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-25T21:23:45-08:00","id":381572,"title":"Thought Experiment: Hypothetical Exigent of Lytek","content":"This hs been bumping around in the back of my head for a while.<br /> <br /> We can extrapolate from Harvest Maiden Janest that an Exigent's powers are a bid more broad than that of the Spirit who crafted their Exaltation-Ten Sheaves was the god of, essentially, &quot;The Harvest of that one specific villages fields&quot; while she herself has powers over &quot;The Harvest&quot;<br /> <br /> So, what powers would a hypothetical Exalted of the God of Exaltation posses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T02:06:41-08:00","id":381705,"title":"","content":"I imagine he'd have a lot of ways to bestow power unto others. Not as much personally mighty as someone who can make those he chooses much greater than they are. Some really badass training and gifting charms. <br /> <br /> Maybe some way to interact with the Past Lives of other Exalted, either to help them recall more clearly or make them forget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T02:59:52-08:00","id":381713,"title":"","content":"Never really thought too much about this before. But taking a few minutes, this is what I came up with.<br /> <br /> Such a hypothetical Exalt would represent the concept of Exaltation itself. They wouldn't necessarily be more powerful than any other Exalt, but their charmset would be inspired by the Exalted, the Exaltations, and the actions that the Exalted have undertaken - specifically the Celestial Exalted more so than Dragon Blooded, as Celestial Exaltation seems to be more Lytek's purview.<br /> <br /> So this charmset would be inspired by both by the greatest wonders that the Exalted host was able to bring into existence, the shining beacon of promise that was the early First Age, as well as the most abject horrors of the First Age so terrible that there was no choice but to forever diminish Creation itself to save it from those same Exalted.<br /> <br /> So charm-wise, I might take some inspiration from Gentimians, whom we have been told have 2 different Essence pools, and the way a given charm functions can change depending on which type of Essence they use to activate the charm.<br /> <br /> I don't know that I would necessarily give this &quot;Chosen of Lytek&quot; two Essence pools, but I would like to have this Exalted's charms dual-function as both &quot;Hero&quot; and &quot;Horror&quot; so that a given charm may be activated in either method. A Hero charm would be representative of the glorious Solars/Lunars/Sidereal heroes and be inspired by the seven virtues, whereas a Horror charm would tend to be representative of the depictions of the negative traits of the Exalted - Solar Tyrants, Lunars Monsters, Traitorous Sidereals, and draw inspiration from the seven deadly sins.<br /> <br /> For a Limit Break system, I would look towards Alchemicals and create a sliding scale for these guys, where they would move between the Hero and Horror aspect, their personality changing as it goes, with one side bringing out the best in them while the other brings out the worst. In either case, they would gain different bonuses and penalties depending on where they are on the scale, so sometimes it might be more advantageous to be a selfish-brigand and other times you'd be better off as a shining knight. Importantly, it would be fairly easy to move (even unintentionally) from one side to the other, so the character would be moving between those two extremes fairly often.<br /> <br /> Well, this idea could probably use some serious ironing out, but that's probably where I would get started if I were to try and whip out a charmset for this Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-26-2015, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T03:07:37-08:00","id":381714,"title":"","content":"He emerged in the East, but his army soon became known across Creation.<br /> In his presence, mere peasants can crush stone with their hands. The frail become tough as oxen, and the dumb may charm kings with their wit. It is said that a light- the scattering, fluid Exaltation within him- enhances their raw Attributes. To be near him is to be near a fountain of energy.<br /> He is never seen on the front lines, and this is well, for his gift is not a personal one. The many folk whose power relies on him protect him loyally, even valiantly. They love him as flowers love the rain.<br /> His will is carried out only by servants, never the man himself. He <i>glowed</i>, my lord, yet beneath that he was only a weak mortal.<br /> In the evenings, he sits around a campfire with his minions, telling them heretical tales of Anathema- and, supposedly, the Heavenly City itself. I...I almost found myself <i>believing</i> his lies, but logic has not failed me. It is impossible for any human, even a Dragon-Blooded, to know what he knows about the past.<br /> Worst of all, he insists that our Chosen are <i>flawed</i>. That a great darkness corrupted the incorruptible Elements long ago, and it makes itself known in terrible sins.<br /> He calls it the 'Great Curse.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T06:09:35-08:00","id":381830,"title":"","content":"I'd probably spin it similar to Fabian Cortez from Marvel Comics. As a mutant, his only &quot;power&quot; was to enhance other mutants.<br /> <br /> He could use this benignly -- when Wolverine stabbed Magneto in the stomach, he &quot;enhanced&quot; Magneto's healing (such that Magneto survived the wounds -- but his body was weak from the unnaturally rapid healing response).<br /> <br /> He could use this malignantly -- when fighting the X-Men, he &quot;enhanced&quot; Bishop's energy-absorption powers (such that he began absorbing all kinds of ambient sources nearby, burning himself out).<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Can't see how it'd fit with a regular troop of characters.<br /> <br /> But possible powers could include....<br /> ....lending motes to others.<br /> ....temporarily lending Essence levels to others (so your Essence 2 Exalted is now Essence 3 for the scene - but you suffer some damage at the end of the scene from burn-out).<br /> ....a mini-suite of defense (defend-other) charms.<br /> ....a mini-suite of social combat charms (for prying in their heads and making you remember/forget things).<br /> <br /> Could also grant a sort of Caliban-style (another mutant) ability to track/spot Exalts (at least those who aren't magically obfuscating their nature). <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> And as an NPC, I'd take even <u>more</u> Marvel inspiration with Apocalypse and his Horsemen. Apocalypse seeks out powerful mutants as his heralds -- and using (cosmic-divine-tech-tools) to empower them, just as he was empowered. An Exigent of Lytek might have a specific plot -- and use her or his abilities to hunt down specific Exalts (who he can then provide with artifacts and aim them at whatever cause he's pushing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T06:47:31-08:00","id":381932,"title":"","content":"I very much intend to play this Exigent at some point.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would go about structuring them as a pure 'support' character in most respects. As the posters above me have suggested, they would primarily work by enhancing the capabilities of other Exalts. I imagine they would work as a fantastic mentor or teacher, actually. A Guru of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I think they could also have some charms for use against other Exalted, but would be particularly weak against anything else. But that's only because I have this image of the guy kicking some Solar butt, then getting killed by an average mortal shortly after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:12:11-08:00","id":381940,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting thought. First, we'd need 3E to really tell us what it is that Lytek specifically does. As it's changed from each edition so far. He isn't actually the God of Exaltation, as his official title is something like God of Power Bestowed Unto Mortals (or something equally innocuous like that). So his Exigent would probably have to bestow certain powers onto others. He could also have charms that bolster other powers used by different people. He might even have some high level charms that grant &quot;power&quot; in a different sense, like declaring some random guy a King of a new kingdom. It's a rather broad, and yet niche category that he controls.<br /> <br /> Not to derail, but I seriously doubt Lytek would ever invest in an exigent. For one, he can't risk disappearing like Ten Sheaves did. From what we know, he's the only one that can do the &quot;pruning&quot; of exaltations for the celestials. I seriously doubt he's taught anyone else to do it, as he was said to take a lot of pride in his personal work with the celestial exalts. Also, most Exigents were claimed to be taken up by gods that really need them to deal with a major threat, or because they feel like their worshippers have forgotten them. Lytek isn't in danger of either of those two reasons. That might help with the direction of your exigent, &quot;why&quot; would Lytek need one to begin with? Just some food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:23:22-08:00","id":381994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=381940#post381940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, most Exigents were claimed to be taken up by gods that really need them to deal with a major threat</div> </div> </div> </div>Going off old editions, I'd say there are 150 nuclear-warheads in the shape of missing Solar Exaltations that would fit the category of &quot;major threat&quot;. Lunar Chimera also fit -- and any rogue Sidereal is a threat, with or without external corruption. Alchemicals would also be an amazing research tool (imagine an unlimited number of custom-built Exaltations?!).<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> More than merely boosting others power, such a character must exist on his own as well. Maybe it can get by with Artifacts and Sorcery and Martial Arts -- presuming it's charm-suite really is focused on enhancing or defending or fixing others.<br /> <br /> Another viable option --- maybe letting it emulate low-level powers (or even pilfering them away temporarily). I mean, there's a Sidereal Martial Art that lets them emulate the animas and some broadly-flavored powers for each Exalt type. You could do a lot of emulation via Mutations (similar to how God-Blooded are built). <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> So the Exigent needs to blend in and track down a Lunar? Kill and consume (X) creatures and then commit (X) motes, where (X) is the number of mutation points you temporarily acquire while committed (so the Exigent now masquerades as a Beastman while exploring the Far East in search of a Chimera).<br /> <br /> Similar tricks for other splats. An Exigent who kills ghost-blooded or consumes ghosts -- and then acquires (X) points for each kill, letting them temporarily carry ghost-blooded merits/flaws (so now they can survive shadowlands better, blend in and track down an Abyssal).<br /> <br /> Something.<br /> <br /> The core aesthetic we seem to have is &quot;enhance others&quot;.<br /> <br /> The sub aesthetic I think could fit is &quot;emulate them so that you can track &amp; hide amongst them&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:39:55-08:00","id":382013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=381994#post381994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going off old editions, I'd say there are 150 nuclear-warheads in the shape of missing Solar Exaltations that would fit the category of &quot;major threat&quot;. Lunar Chimera also fit -- and any rogue Sidereal is a threat, with or without external corruption. Alchemicals would also be an amazing research tool (imagine an unlimited number of custom-built Exaltations?!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except none of those are actually threats to him or his purview. Ten Sheaves fields (his purview and very existence was based on) were threatened by the fey. They would have been Wyld-tainted at best, or complete unmade at worst. His very existence would come to an end if he did nothing. So he risked his existence (better then being guaranteed destruction) and created an Exigent. The 150 corrupted Solars, Lunar chimera, and rogue Sidereals in no way threated Lytek's continued existence. While he's annoyed about the Solar corruption (and theirs hints he's taking actions to attempt a fix), the Lunar chimera that are killed immediately return to his purview. Sidereals that die, even Rakan Thulio if/when he dies, still return to his cabinet upon death.<br /> <br /> Also remember that Lytek's purview isn't exalts, it's Mortals Bestowed with Power (or something like that). The existence of the Alchemicals, while surprising, would actual expand upon his purview. Lytek isn't threatened and has no real need to create an Exigent at the moment. Now if your running that in your particular game, that's theirs a threat to him, then I could see his need for an Exigent. I was curious if Rater had given any thought to the nature of the threat, or some other reason that Lytek would take the risk of creating an exigent?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: Just thought of something that might be interesting. What if Lytek thought an Exigent with his power could cleanse the corrupted Solars! Do you think he'd be willing to take the chance on an Exigent if he thought it meant fixing the corrupted Solars? Or, what if he determined that a Exigent of Bestowed Power might be capable of cleansing the Great Curse on all the Celestial Exalts, he might consider such a sacrifice to be his duty?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-26-2015, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:50:13-08:00","id":382024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=381940#post381940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting thought. First, we'd need 3E to really tell us what it is that Lytek specifically does. As it's changed from each edition so far. He isn't actually the God of Exaltation, as his official title is something like God of Power Bestowed Unto Mortals (or something equally innocuous like that).<br /> <br /> Also remember that Lytek's purview isn't exalts, it's Mortals Bestowed with Power (or something like that).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're thinking of Parad, God of Inherited Might. Lytek is, and has always been, God of Exaltation. His purview has always been Exaltation. Given that concepts such as War and Peace get their own gods, it's only fitting that Exaltation gets one too, though Lytek's execution varies depending on the author and whether you're talking about Lytek as-printed or Lytek as the fans think he is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:50:52-08:00","id":382026,"title":"","content":"I would have memory manipulation in there as part of their charm suite, a major part of it actually. From what I can remember of Lytek's actual job function, he was mainly supposed to remove and add memories to make the next generation of exalts better at care taking creation or some such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:14:57-08:00","id":382057,"title":"","content":"It'd be broken but also make sense that he can learn other Exalt's charms like an Eclipsoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:18:09-08:00","id":382088,"title":"","content":"I gave this some thought when it first came out and concluded that, although it's one of the first concepts to come to mind, it's also one of the worst possible things to make an Exigent for, and there's <i>probably </i>no way to do it well. That said, if I were going to do it, it'd be a behind-the-scenes wise mentor figure, sort of an extrapolation of the philosophy you see in Throne Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:30:56-08:00","id":382100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382024#post382024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you're thinking of Parad, God of Inherited Might. Lytek is, and has always been, God of Exaltation. His purview has always been Exaltation. Given that concepts such as War and Peace get their own gods, it's only fitting that Exaltation gets one too, though Lytek's execution varies depending on the author and whether you're talking about Lytek as-printed or Lytek as the fans think he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm misremembering, but I don't recall if God of Exaltation was his title. In 1E he supposedly had some power over who an exaltation went too (can't confirm as I never played 1E). In 2E he had no power what-so-ever over Exaltation. His only job as far as Exalts go, is to prune celestial exalts memories as they pass from host to host. I remember a similar argument in another thread a while back. What it boiled down to is their was a difference between Bestowed Power and Inherited Power. Though it was a while ago, and I can't recall if the Devs said anything about 3Es outlook.<br /> <br /> Perhaps he is the 3E God of Exaltation now. Couldn't tell you one way or the other now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:34:09-08:00","id":382102,"title":"","content":"His title in Compass: Yu-shan is the Right Hand of Power and God of Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:42:08-08:00","id":382106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382102#post382102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His title in Compass: Yu-shan is the Right Hand of Power and God of Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So one more reason I said he needs to be clarified in 3E. Being a God of Exaltation and having absolutely no power over his purview is ridiculous. He needs a job that he has some affect on other &quot;oh so he's why I remember your face but not your name from 1000 years ago&quot;!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:50:05-08:00","id":382111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382100#post382100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I'm misremembering, but I don't recall if God of Exaltation was his title. In 1E he supposedly had some power over who an exaltation went too (can't confirm as I never played 1E). In 2E he had no power what-so-ever over Exaltation. His only job as far as Exalts go, is to prune celestial exalts memories as they pass from host to host. I remember a similar argument in another thread a while back. What it boiled down to is their was a difference between Bestowed Power and Inherited Power. Though it was a while ago, and I can't recall if the Devs said anything about 3Es outlook.<br /> <br /> Perhaps he is the 3E God of Exaltation now. Couldn't tell you one way or the other now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted: the Sidereals (1e) and Compass: Yu-Shan (2e) both have Lytek as God of Exaltation, the Right Hand of Power.<br /> <br /> He never truly had any power over where Exaltations went or to whom, or any true influence over the process of Exaltation, though some authors (notably in MoXP: Abyssals) believed he had to bless a candidate before the Exaltation would accept them and successfully join. He always pruned memories, believing that it shaped the resulting Exalt in demeanor, outlook, and eventually endeavor; consequently, he had a paternal attitude towards Celestial Exalts, since he knew them intimately. His cabinet, rather than being a gilded cage for Exaltations, was more of an open-air roost where Exaltations rested and resided. Lytek, as a symbol and a theme, represents the idea that Exaltation is instrument and instrumentality, and he's the face for the idea that Exaltation places one into a long lineage of machinations reaching back centuries.<br /> <br /> Pretty much anyone who didn't grasp that imagery ended up misunderstanding the entire concept of Lytek, which unfortunately includes a lot of people. Take a look at that previous thread, with people reacting poorly to the <i>idea </i>that there's a God of Exaltation. The comparison to a river god is apt - a river god, even a god of all rivers, has no real power over rivers or the concept of such, but they can certainly do things that are hugely abnormal or unique that none others can. The idea of someone having a unique relationship to a character's glowing signifier of heroism, deeper in some ways than the character themselves, can be enormously insulting to the setting unless it's properly handled. On occasion, someone would object to the idea that memories of past lives does a more personable job of placing a character into that lineage of heroism possessed by past bearers of their Exaltation, but you can't well punch a memory in the face.<br /> <br /> It's strange what one remembers; in the past, I'd done a lot of research on Lytek, because I was always supremely fond of him and because I'd hoped to write an Ink Monkeys article on him, to further expand upon the roost concept and discuss the idea of Lytek as a sculptor of divine heroism. I was about 5k in when the Ink Monkeys disbanded. I've no idea what Lytek's relationship to Exaltation will be, especially since the concept of Exaltation has changed so much from 1e and 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 01-26-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:55:45-08:00","id":382116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being a God of Exaltation and having absolutely no power over his purview is ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>Again, I think the idea that not being able to reclaim an Exaltation or Exalt whomever he pleases constitutes &quot;no power&quot; over a purview is a failure of imagination, honestly. The God of the Mississippi River can't go make another Mississippi River - there's only one. Nor can he destroy said River without destroying his power. But he can stop it from flooding and control where the silt deposits go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:04:12-08:00","id":382119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382111#post382111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted: the Sidereals (1e) and Compass: Yu-Shan (2e) both have Lytek as God of Exaltation, the Right Hand of Power.<br /> <br /> He never truly had any power over where Exaltations went or to whom, or any true influence over the process of Exaltation, though some authors (notably in MoXP: Abyssals) believed he had to bless a candidate before the Exaltation would accept them and successfully join. He always pruned memories, believing that it shaped the resulting Exalt in demeanor, outlook, and eventually endeavor; consequently, he had a paternal attitude towards Celestial Exalts, since he knew them intimately. His cabinet, rather than being a gilded cage for Exaltations, was more of an open-air roost where Exaltations rested and resided. Lytek, as a symbol and a theme, represents the idea that Exaltation is instrument and instrumentality, and he's the face for the idea that Exaltation places one into a long lineage of machinations reaching back centuries.<br /> <br /> Pretty much anyone who didn't grasp that imagery ended up misunderstanding the entire concept of Lytek, which unfortunately included a number of writers and developers, not to mention a significant portion of the vocal fanbase. Take a look at that previous thread, with people reacting poorly to the <i>idea </i>that there's a God of Exaltation. The comparison to a river god is apt - a river god, even a god of all rivers, has no real power over rivers or the concept of such, but they can certainly do things that are hugely abnormal or unique that none others can. The idea of someone having a unique relationship to a character's glowing signifier of heroism, deeper in some ways than the character themselves, can be enormously insulting to the setting unless it's properly handled. On occasion, someone would object to the idea that memories of past lives does a more personable job of placing a character into that lineage of heroism possessed by past bearers of their Exaltation, but you can't well punch a memory in the face.<br /> <br /> It's strange what one remembers; in the past, I'd done a lot of research on Lytek, because I was always supremely fond of him and because I'd hoped to write an Ink Monkeys article on him, to further expand upon the roost concept and discuss the idea of Lytek as a sculptor of divine heroism. I was about 5k in when the Ink Monkeys disbanded. I've no idea what Lytek's relationship to Exaltation will be, especially since the concept of Exaltation has changed so much from 1e and 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that. It does help clarify some things. What I remember about the &quot;Bestowed Power vs Inherited Power&quot; thread, was that it got a bit to vocal from a hostile crowd. Which is why I quit following it. I can have strong beliefs, but I'm not gonna bludgeon people with them.<br /> <br /> With your explanation of Lytek, I'm not sure what to do with this Exigent. I still don't see a valid threat to him or his purview in the current lore (though 3E could change that). I'm at an even greater loss of what kind of powers his Exigent might have. Perhaps something along the lines of granting minor powers that change a persons destiny. Perhaps a charm set based on making small alterations to someone's Destiny, allowing them to grow into something more then they would have been.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-26-2015, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:42:52-08:00","id":382135,"title":"","content":"I don't think we really need to focus on the reason that Lytek would need an Exigent for the purposes of this thread since it's just a thought experiment anyway and if someone really needed a motivation for it, they could just consult their ST on the matter.<br /> <br /> I am by no means an expert on Lytek and only really have cursory knowledge of him, but from what I've gathered in this thread and what I've heard around, makes me think that his charms would definitely have a component of lifting up others, especially mortals. Maybe blessing them with temporary attribute or ability dots or, for higher essence charms, permanent increases. In terms of interacting with other Exalted, he could probably give them smaller power boosts as well and, given Lytek's duties as god, maybe interact with the past lives of a particular exaltation or help an exalt remember things from past lives.<br /> <br /> I think he should also have some combat charms so in keeping with the theme of exaltation, maybe charms that do different or more things against enemies with higher essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T11:04:34-08:00","id":382147,"title":"","content":"Lytek isn't merely trying to fix Exaltations, like some kooky professor trying to perfect his bug collection.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted were imprisoned for an epoch (and thus out of his purview). Now half of them are corrupted (outside of his control -- and terrifying enough that if more people realized what the Abyssals and Infernals really are, they might agree that imprisoning them all was wise in the first place). <br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are inherently corrupted by Wyld exposure (their 2nd Age versions are verifiably broken when compared to their 1st Age variants). If I were in his position, I would be <i>seriously</i> concerned about their future mutation. What comes next? The went from 5 to 3 castes -- why not 3 to 1? Why have castes at all? How about they accelerate the &quot;tattoo-less shapeshifting turns me into a hybrid god-monster&quot; so it can be a nice curse instead of empowerment?<br /> <br /> You're right that Sidereals are fine -- I'd still be worried about them, considering that the Bronze ones mugged me ; and they're so rare and few in number that any corruption is an entire percentage point. And as the Reclamation depicted, they're a lot easier to round-up if targeting. They're also the weakest ones (in that they're Destined from Birth --- so if someone knew which baby was going to turn Sidereal, you got an entire decade to kidnap a weakling and can imprison them in unaging crystal as soon as they hit adolescence).<br /> <br /> TLDR Version:<br /> <br /> Exaltations have already been messed with in the setting. They don't regrow, they don't breed, they don't heal themselves. Tell me that my entire existence is predicated on cultivating 700 irreplaceable works of art and I would be <u>very</u> attentive to those 700, especially after seeing 150 of them stolen and vandalized, 300 of them partially melted by the Wyld, and knowing that the other 100 are all made of glass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382013#post382013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>EDIT: Just thought of something that might be interesting. What if Lytek thought an Exigent with his power could cleanse the corrupted Solars! Do you think he'd be willing to take the chance on an Exigent if he thought it meant fixing the corrupted Solars? Or, what if he determined that a Exigent of Bestowed Power might be capable of cleansing the Great Curse on all the Celestial Exalts, he might consider such a sacrifice to be his duty?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of where I was going with what I said afterward regarding different &quot;Blooded&quot; types.<br /> <br /> An Exigent with the right toolkit might be more competent at sneaking around and spying on all the big bads - and Exalts - that Lytek has a keen interest in. Actual Exalts tend to be hard to control (and self-serving); Sidereals also take an interest in this job (but their powers turn shitty outside of Creation). <br /> <br /> I mean.... how can someone seriously say that..... the God of Exalting mortals..... would have no interest in Exalting mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T11:32:41-08:00","id":382163,"title":"","content":"I sorta got a mental image of an Exalt that can touch you and turn you into a Half-Caste type Godblooded, due to using an understanding of the nature of the exaltation to recreate their power in part with mortal essence but being unable to create the exaltation whole cloth.<br /> <br /> Of course, since Godbloods have their own charms instead of spirit/demon/raksha/exalt charms now, what effect being a Halfe-Caste would have is up for debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T12:42:16-08:00","id":382210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382147#post382147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lytek isn't merely trying to fix Exaltations, like some kooky professor trying to perfect his bug collection.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted were imprisoned for an epoch (and thus out of his purview). Now half of them are corrupted (outside of his control -- and terrifying enough that if more people realized what the Abyssals and Infernals really are, they might agree that imprisoning them all was wise in the first place).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree he'd definitely like to cleanse the corrupted Solars (ie Abyssals &amp; Infernals), and he'd definitely like to see the Great Curse get removed. I'm not sure he's worried about what would happen if more people discovered what the Abyssals and Infernals really are though. As for make a case that it was wise to lock them up, their being locked up is precisely the reason they could even be corrupted. It could also be stated that attempting the same thing again with the Solars, or any other Celestial Exalts, could very well expand upon the enemies of Creation!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382147#post382147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar Exalted are inherently corrupted by Wyld exposure (their 2nd Age versions are verifiably broken when compared to their 1st Age variants). If I were in his position, I would be <i>seriously</i> concerned about their future mutation. What comes next? The went from 5 to 3 castes -- why not 3 to 1? Why have castes at all? How about they accelerate the &quot;tattoo-less shapeshifting turns me into a hybrid god-monster&quot; so it can be a nice curse instead of empowerment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta wonder how this might work, since the Lunar's apparently don't have the connection to the Wyld in 3E that they did in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382147#post382147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean.... how can someone seriously say that..... the God of Exalting mortals..... would have no interest in Exalting mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if this was aimed at me, as I don't recall ever saying Lytek has no interest in Exalting mortals. I just said that we know Exigents &quot;can&quot; pretty much destroy the Exalting god. Lytek has a duty that he's quite proud of doing. Even Lytek isn't going to risk destruction for no reason. All I asked was, did the OP have a reason in mind. I also said it was just something for the OP to think about. Regardless it wouldn't change the Exigents abilities, but would give us some background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382147#post382147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sorta got a mental image of an Exalt that can touch you and turn you into a Half-Caste type Godblooded, due to using an understanding of the nature of the exaltation to recreate their power in part with mortal essence but being unable to create the exaltation whole cloth.<br /> <br /> Of course, since Godbloods have their own charms instead of spirit/demon/raksha/exalt charms now, what effect being a Halfe-Caste would have is up for debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely something to think about. Do we even know if &quot;Half-Castes&quot; exist in 3E? Since enlightened mortals are out, I see Lytek's exigent having the ability to boost attributes and/or stats for mortals. Building off the memories thing Lytek does, perhaps awakening former memories of a past life to increase the number of skills the mortal has. Imagine awakening memories of a farmers life as a mercenary, it would add whole new skill sets to the character. He might also be capable of helping Exalts remember more of their past. Perhaps even &quot;borrow&quot; a bit of the Exalts power and transfer it to someone else (or use it himself). <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T12:44:55-08:00","id":382214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382147#post382147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar Exalted were imprisoned for an epoch (and thus out of his purview). Now half of them are corrupted (outside of his control -- and terrifying enough that if more people realized what the Abyssals and Infernals really are, they might agree that imprisoning them all was wise in the first place).<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are inherently corrupted by Wyld exposure (their 2nd Age versions are verifiably broken when compared to their 1st Age variants). If I were in his position, I would be <i>seriously</i> concerned about their future mutation. What comes next? The went from 5 to 3 castes -- why not 3 to 1? Why have castes at all? How about they accelerate the &quot;tattoo-less shapeshifting turns me into a hybrid god-monster&quot; so it can be a nice curse instead of empowerment?<br /> <br /> You're right that Sidereals are fine -- I'd still be worried about them, considering that the Bronze ones mugged me ; and they're so rare and few in number that any corruption is an entire percentage point. And as the Reclamation depicted, they're a lot easier to round-up if targeting. They're also the weakest ones (in that they're Destined from Birth --- so if someone knew which baby was going to turn Sidereal, you got an entire decade to kidnap a weakling and can imprison them in unaging crystal a</div> </div> </div> </div>You're basing a lot of worry on some of the worst fluff written in the setting. Stuff that is incredibly unlikely to return in the new edition.<br /> <br /> I suggest not doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T12:49:26-08:00","id":382215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382119#post382119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for that. It does help clarify some things. What I remember about the &quot;Bestowed Power vs Inherited Power&quot; thread, was that it got a bit to vocal from a hostile crowd. Which is why I quit following it. I can have strong beliefs, but I'm not gonna bludgeon people with them.<br /> <br /> With your explanation of Lytek, I'm not sure what to do with this Exigent. I still don't see a valid threat to him or his purview in the current lore (though 3E could change that). I'm at an even greater loss of what kind of powers his Exigent might have. Perhaps something along the lines of granting minor powers that change a persons destiny. Perhaps a charm set based on making small alterations to someone's Destiny, allowing them to grow into something more then they would have been.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What could be used as a good threat for Lytek is him getting wind of another jade prison, fake or not he won't like the idea of being smacked around by sidereals again and it would probably push him just enough to start working on his own exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:03:59-08:00","id":382222,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382111#post382111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On occasion, someone would object to the idea that memories of past lives does a more personable job of placing a character into that lineage of heroism possessed by past bearers of their Exaltation, but you can't well punch a memory in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another part of that immaculate memory (as far as the Infernal Exalted are concerned, especially) is that raw, unedited memories mean you can go to sleep every night remembering how you were murdered; how many cities you destroyed; how many horrific things you faced and are now underpowered to survive (and the sheer paranoia that will create). You also have the situation of Exalted rivalries -- wasn't it Salina whose Exaltation died in the Primordial War to SHE WHO LIVES IN HER NAME -- and as a result, decided to <i>rewrite all of reality to defy hierarchy</i>, as a way to slight the Primordial-turned-Yozi?<br /> <br /> So editing memories is a damn important job, IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382119#post382119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps something along the lines of granting minor powers that change a persons destiny. Perhaps a charm set based on making small alterations to someone's Destiny, allowing them to grow into something more then they would have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Martial Art in Imperfect Lotus that lets mortals increase their Destiny background (which is apparently one of the things that Exaltation seeks out). So maybe you run around, teach kung fu, guiding potential Exalts long before they realize they were being guided and might Exalt. <br /> <br /> But as aforementioned - threats. Out of a mere 700, 450 Exaltations are a mess right now (either Infernal &amp; Abyssal - and outside his control ; or Lunar and permanently warped). He might be 100% okay with the 150 Solars, but then he has another 100 (Sidereals) who have directly messed with his purview in the past; who directly tried to prevent others from Exalted (Jade Prison); and who are themselves overtaxed and vulnerable for a decade before Exalting again.<br /> <br /> Plenty to worry about. I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:09:52-08:00","id":382224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382215#post382215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could be used as a good threat for Lytek is him getting wind of another jade prison, fake or not he won't like the idea of being smacked around by sidereals again and it would probably push him just enough to start working on his own exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a Jade Prison is unlikely. Not impossible, just really difficult in the current setting. Lytek has round the clock protection from Celestial Lions due to what the Sidereals did last time. Also, the Sids had to break the Mask to get away with what they did last time. I'm not sure there's anything specific that would allow them to do something so highly illegal and get away with it a second time (the Maidens supposedly placed guards on all the constellations).<br /> <br /> It does give me another interesting idea. What if Lytek discovered that an enterprising Twilight had discovered the whole truth of what the Sidereals did. He might be inclined to build an Orichalcum Prison to toss all the Sids in for proper recompense (I &quot;may&quot; have attempted this once as a Twilight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). While Lytek might initially find it amusing, he wouldn't want to lose anymore Celestial Exalts to petty revenge. That might be a good reason to create an Exigent. I also still like the idea of working to cleanse the Great Curse and Abyssal/Infernal corruption. Who knows, maybe the combination to a lot of little problems could give him reason to create an Exigent to help clean it all up. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:14:20-08:00","id":382229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382224#post382224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does give me another interesting idea. What if Lytek discovered that an enterprising Twilight had discovered the whole truth of what the Sidereals did. </div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Here is this total perfect evidence-blocking effect which forever changed the laws of the cosmos...that a Twilight circumvented, probably with Charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> See how that looks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:21:31-08:00","id":382231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382222#post382222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnother part of that immaculate memory (as far as the Infernal Exalted are concerned, especially) is that raw, unedited memories mean you can go to sleep every night remembering how you were murdered; how many cities you destroyed; how many horrific things you faced and are now underpowered to survive (and the sheer paranoia that will create). You also have the situation of Exalted rivalries -- wasn't it Salina whose Exaltation died in the Primordial War to SHE WHO LIVES IN HER NAME -- and as a result, decided to <i>rewrite all of reality to defy hierarchy</i>, as a way to slight the Primordial-turned-Yozi?<br /> <br /> So editing memories is a damn important job, IMO.<br /> <br /> There's a Martial Art in Imperfect Lotus that lets mortals increase their Destiny background (which is apparently one of the things that Exaltation seeks out). So maybe you run around, teach kung fu, guiding potential Exalts long before they realize they were being guided and might Exalt.<br /> <br /> But as aforementioned - threats. Out of a mere 700, 450 Exaltations are a mess right now (either Infernal &amp; Abyssal - and outside his control ; or Lunar and permanently warped). He might be 100% okay with the 150 Solars, but then he has another 100 (Sidereals) who have directly messed with his purview in the past; who directly tried to prevent others from Exalted (Jade Prison); and who are themselves overtaxed and vulnerable for a decade before Exalting again.<br /> <br /> Plenty to worry about. I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the perfect martial arts for Lytek's exigent to take up!<br /> <br /> As for the others, the biggest issue is we don't know &quot;if&quot; the Lunars are corrupted anymore. Supposedly they have very little to do with the Wyld anymore. So chimerism, assuming it's still a thing, may be more internal to their own exaltation then any type of corruption. There are a lot of questions I have about Lunars, and I'm thinking of starting a separate thread to discuss them more in depth. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:31:55-08:00","id":382383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=382210#post382210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely something to think about. Do we even know if &quot;Half-Castes&quot; exist in 3E? Since enlightened mortals are out, I see Lytek's exigent having the ability to boost attributes and/or stats for mortals. Building off the memories thing Lytek does, perhaps awakening former memories of a past life to increase the number of skills the mortal has. Imagine awakening memories of a farmers life as a mercenary, it would add whole new skill sets to the character. He might also be capable of helping Exalts remember more of their past. Perhaps even &quot;borrow&quot; a bit of the Exalts power and transfer it to someone else (or use it himself).</div> </div> </div> </div>What We Know says that The Childen of Celestial Exalts will have some kind of power, though not if they'l count as &quot;God Blooded&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:01:18-08:00","id":382408,"title":"","content":"I'm content to wait until the relevant books are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:49:40-08:00","id":383800,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking about this earlier. Here's my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Lytek isn't just a generic god of Exaltation; he interacts with Exaltations in specific ways. In particular, his domain seems very focused on dealing with the eternal reincarnation aspect of Exaltation and the memories associated with it. Therefore, I would probably have an Exigent of Lytek focus primarily on that particular aspect of Exaltations.<br /> <br /> They would have powers to help others recover memories and (temporarily or as a form of training) skills from past lives. They'd have charms to identify past lives and gather information using them, to track Exaltations through the ages and sense or manipulate the connections between them. They could help other Exalted unlock their true potential in various ways, often by using past-life memories as a form of training. Their social charms could focus on evoking or manipulating intimacies from past lives. And so on.<br /> <br /> Possibly this focus on reincarnation could be part of how the Exigent's exaltation works. It should reincarnate itself, probably, but beyond that it might choose hosts whose mortal souls had been Exalted or otherwise exceptional in a past life, and allow them to access some of the skills and power from that past (<i>not</i>, of course, generally in the form of actual Exalted charms -- except maybe a small list of whitelisted stuff -- but things like being able to develop their own Exigent-of-Lytek swordsmanship charms based around a thematic of calling on swordsmanship skill from a past life as an Exalt.)<br /> <br /> They'd probably also have a few charms related to the process of Exaltation or for interacting with the Exalted, mostly informational in nature (because manipulating Exaltations directly is generally not doable) -- charms to imprecisely detect people who are likely to Exalt, charms to sense the presence of the Exalted and so on.<br /> <br /> Of course, they should have <i>some</i> charms to empower mortals -- akin to the Solar charm Power Awarding Prana in some ways, maybe -- since that's central enough to the thematic of Exaltation that you couldn't really make an Exigent of Lytek without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-27-2015, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T17:39:34-08:00","id":383842,"title":"","content":"They would probably get ganked by someone who felt threatened by another exalt who might be able to alter their exaltation. I'd imagine that in particular the Deathlords and denizens of Malfeas wouldn't appreciate someone running around who might be able to undo the alterations they worked so hard to make to solar exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T19:34:34-08:00","id":383898,"title":"","content":"That's what Lytek does, but not what he is.<br /> <br /> Tending to memories the way he does is more like a hobby-his official job is apparently making sure it goes smoothly and that one incarnations personality or memories doesn't override the next guy.<br /> <br /> He also apparently has an instinctual understanding of how Exaltations work-He and Nara-o* are apparently the only two beings within fate that know of the great curse. charms derived from the Exigent having a similar understanding should also probably be a thing, though I'm not sure how that'd work.<br /> <br /> I suggested &quot;Use understanding of Exalted Essence to turn mortals into Half-Cates&quot; but I'm not sure if Half-Castes are still a thing or how they'd work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:06:13-08:00","id":383955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383898#post383898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggested &quot;Use understanding of Exalted Essence to turn mortals into Half-Cates&quot; but I'm not sure if Half-Castes are still a thing or how they'd work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but think that the power to uplift mortals in that way is pretty OP no matter the mechanics. You now have an Exigent capable of creating supernatural followers or allies. That sounds really strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:10:58-08:00","id":383969,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for something back in mid-2e--it had started as a thought of a sort of meta-martial art--which I think will probably see implementation as the Exigent of Lytek eventually in my game:<br /> <br /> It's less that any one incarnation is an apt reflector of Lytek so much as they form a lineage of power: Each one starts off bearing the charms and trappings, and sobriquet of his predecessor, but in time develops his own idiom, forging his own legend. Upon death, they leave an echo of themselves as a god who mentors their successor for a time.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I know there are problems there, but it's still something I'm going to do, most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:17:04-08:00","id":383971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383955#post383955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but think that the power to uplift mortals in that way is pretty OP no matter the mechanics. You now have an Exigent capable of creating supernatural followers or allies. That sounds really strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Solar Lore charm that turn a person into an Enlightened Mortal require you to commit a shit load of motes, you just need to slap this on Lytek's Exigent's charm to prevent him from mass producing a magic army.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:41:29-08:00","id":383989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383955#post383955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but think that the power to uplift mortals in that way is pretty OP no matter the mechanics. You now have an Exigent capable of creating supernatural followers or allies. That sounds really strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Limits on how many you can do at a time-I imagine altering a mortals essence enough for them to count as half-castes might take time. Also, if god-blooded aren't getting spirit charms, I doubt Half-casts, if they continue in the form they ave currently, as a type of god-blooded, would have Exalt Charms.<br /> <br /> Lets say for the purpose of this discussion, a Half-caste is a God-blooded whose god-blooded charms and/or mutations are influenced by the themes of their exalted parents rather than by whatever god/elemental/demon/ghost/fae/other is there parent-They wouldn't have Exalt Charms, but their God Blooded Charms would be similar in nature.<br /> <br /> Now, if Technician of the Exalted Light invests some of his essence into a mortal, and spends a month or two reshaping that mortal's essence to resemble a... let's say a Lunar's, because I've got them on the brain, a Lunar's essence, and turns that mortal into a mortal half-caste. Now, let's say that empowering the mortal like this is a might feet-the pinnacle of the skill derived from inheriting Lytek's understanding of the nature of the Exaltations and the process of exalting, so lets make it an essence 5 charm. Let's also say that even though you're just making them a half-caste, their soul still has to resonate with the the nature of the Exaltation-the kind of person who would exalt as a Lunar if put in a situation where Lunar Exaltation is a possible outcome.<br /> <br /> Now, lets say that the mortal's altered essence is unstable, so the Chosen of Lytek has to comic a significant number of motes and can't reclaim them until the Half-caste's essence stabilizes-let's say the Half-Cast starts as essence one and stabilizes when they reach essence two-reclaim the committed mosts before then, and the half-caste reverts to a mortal.<br /> <br /> so, the quality of the followers the half caste can train up and empower is greater, but is restricted in how fast the quantity can grow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T22:04:34-08:00","id":383998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383971#post383971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Solar Lore charm that turn a person into an Enlightened Mortal require you to commit a shit load of motes, you just need to slap this on Lytek's Exigent's charm to prevent him from mass producing a magic army.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be boring to copy Power-Awarding Prana <i>exactly</i>, of course. (And also, it's not, I think, a charm that sees much use, whereas empowering mortals should be one of the defining things you do.)<br /> <br /> One alternative would be to limit the number of mortals they can empower at once, then give them an entire charm tree for interacting with these empowered proteges. You'd also have to answer the question of what, exactly, these mortals get -- you can't give them Chosen of Lytek charms, I think, for a variety of reasons. But limiting the number you can have at once solves the main problem you get (where people can just grow in power limitlessly by empowering unlimited servants) -- then you just have to factor the total power of the empowered disciples it can produce into the charm itself.<br /> <br /> Also, one major difference from Power-Awarding Prana should be that you can't revoke your choice of a mortal (since that's how Exaltation works, and this is based on its themes.) You're stuck with the disciples you empower, at least until they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-28-2015, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T23:04:41-08:00","id":384007,"title":"","content":"Perhaps make it so the Chosen of Lytek does not empower them, but rather, the Chosen of Lytek acts as a conduit?<br /> <br /> So he must find an Exalted, and then use his Lytek-Charms to filter the Exalt's power into the Mortals. It gives a reason for the Chosen of Lytek to associate with and seek Exalts, and since he has the ability to help them find their inner memories and train, a Chosen of Lytek can specifically look for someone who has great techniques hidden inside of them, make those manifest, and THEN dole these out.<br /> <br /> Hell, perhaps even be able to do it between Gods, and stranger things, and Men, rather than just Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T00:41:09-08:00","id":384042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383998#post383998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be boring to copy Power-Awarding Prana <i>exactly</i>, of course. (And also, it's not, I think, a charm that sees much use, whereas empowering mortals should be one of the defining things you do.)<br /> <br /> One alternative would be to limit the number of mortals they can empower at once, then give them an entire charm tree for interacting with these empowered proteges. You'd also have to answer the question of what, exactly, these mortals get -- you can't give them Chosen of Lytek charms, I think, for a variety of reasons. But limiting the number you can have at once solves the main problem you get (where people can just grow in power limitlessly by empowering unlimited servants) -- then you just have to factor the total power of the empowered disciples it can produce into the charm itself.<br /> <br /> Also, one major difference from Power-Awarding Prana should be that you can't revoke your choice of a mortal (since that's how Exaltation works, and this is based on its themes.) You're stuck with the disciples you empower, at least until they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe an empowered human wouldn't get actual charms but would just gain the ability to do 'basic' exalt things like ignore mundane infections and heal faster and such? I'd imagine a lot of heroic mortals would kill just to get those things most exalts don't even think about anymore after they start learning charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T05:51:41-08:00","id":384152,"title":"","content":"Path of the Arbiter dudes.<br /> <br /> Via Meditation on the Heart, they can channel actions through their Virtues - and turn dice gained into successes.<br /> Forging the... Soul-Born Sword, Armor of Integrity, Bond of Fellowship....all let you gain magical weapons, armor and familiars.<br /> Meditation on Judgment lets you swear foes into surrendering, binding them akin to Eclipse Caste oaths -- or letting the Arbiter do aggravated damage against the foul wretch.<br /> The charms all reward you for having higher Virtues (the more Virtuous, the stronger the powers).<br /> And not only have Sidereals &quot;thrown a blessing&quot; over them as a whole - but through it, mortals can buy the Destiny background.<br /> <br /> Exigent travels Creation.<br /> Exigent teaches kung-fu.<br /> Kung-fu masters become more worthy of Exaltation (or maybe of being turned into God-Blooded or Exigents or whatever).<br /> Win/win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T06:16:35-08:00","id":384163,"title":"","content":"All I know is that I'm not really keen on an Exalted concept whose only power is to enhance others,<br /> I don't know what limitations the new Exalts introduced in 3rd edition might have, but being forced into a support role like that seems overly narrow and somewhat contrary to my expectations of what it means to be Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T07:46:35-08:00","id":384206,"title":"","content":"Man, I don't know if I agree with that.<br /> <br /> Ever played SMITE? It's a free MOBA (Massive Online Battle Arena) in which gods from different pantheons are all beating the poop out of each other. My friends always teased me because they had better Kill / Death / Assist ratios -- and the better those are, the more xp and gold you get, allowing you to power up faster and thus kill even more! <b><u>BUT</u></b> to me (and the mechanics of the game) - 10, 100, 1000 kills won't actually win you a match. The end-goal are the Objectives (first destroy the defensive Towers -- then you can reach and kill the enemy teams' Titan).<br /> <br /> So I'll play Aphrodite (whose chief abilities involve healing herself &amp; her partner ; stunning enemies with a kiss (and giving your partner a damage bonus, due to jealousy) ; improving you &amp; your partners speed and mana regen ; providing temporary immunity to both of you ; and one negligible damage ability. She's PURE SUPPORT. My K/D/A ratio is terrible. But my partner runs around like a Lunar DBT on Cocaine thanks to me.<br /> <br /> Or I play Hel (whose chief abilities involve AoE heals, damage to extras, a few other buffs) and purchase pure AoE items (favoring empowering friends over myself) and they grudgingly bitch a lot less (because none of them are going to offend the person keeping them alive).<br /> <br /> Or the old Nu Wa kit -- which was predominantly a PVE one. Early game, I'd get curb-stomped and the strangers with the higher kills would disparage me -- but late game, I often did more Siege Damage (against Towers &amp; Titan - the goals of winning) than the entire Enemy Team (5) and the rest of my team (4) <u>combined</u>. While everyone else fights battles, I fight the battleground and reshape the flow of the fight (and with each fallen Tower, my allies are getting boosts to gold and moral too).<br /> <br /> TLDR Version:<br /> <br /> People who enjoy Support roles find it very challenging -- very fun -- and more interesting than being another SUPER KILLBOT PRINCESS.<br /> <br /> Hell, I designed an entire Devil Tiger around the &quot;Defend Other&quot; keyword and &quot;Intimacies&quot; --- an entire kit that would only work to benefit Intimacies (even if they're enemies) or with huge vulnerabilities (so even a hated enemy could bypass defenses or ignore offensive charms in this kit). It was <u>fun</u> -- support roles require a lot more planning and countering than mere &quot;I spend 2 motes, I stab him dead&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T08:39:19-08:00","id":384250,"title":"","content":"I'm not questioning if a support role can be fun, I'm questioning if pure support is a good place to go for a type of exalt. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T08:54:33-08:00","id":384260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384250#post384250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not questioning if a support role can be fun, I'm questioning if pure support is a good place to go for a type of exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>For an Exigent, it probably is.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, not every Exalt type has to be flexible enough to accommodate a wide range of playstyles. I always thought that the Solars were necessarily the broadest in their conceptual space, whereas the various other splats tend to have narrower themes because their powers tend to let them do things that are more specific or because they exist in a more clearly defined social context.<br /> <br /> Given how Exigents as a group are the &quot;Choose Your Own Homebrewed Powerset&quot; Exalted, it seems to me that any given exigent only needs to be as broad as the one player using it demands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:10:53-08:00","id":384268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384250#post384250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not questioning if a support role can be fun, I'm questioning if pure support is a good place to go for a type of exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can make a solid Solar with this premise, and especially a Sidereal, so I think it's doable. It's a different sort of spotlight, and absolutely a bit unconventional, but I wouldn't go so far as to take it off the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:23:22-08:00","id":384276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384268#post384268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make a solid Solar with this premise, and especially a Sidereal, so I think it's doable. It's a different sort of spotlight, and absolutely a bit unconventional, but I wouldn't go so far as to take it off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Lioness is questioning an individual within a type of Exalted pursuing such an approach, more the idea of an entire Exalted type being oriented toward that approach alone. For my part, I'm inclined to agree with semicasual that I don't think it's a problem for some Exalted, by way of Exigents or other homebrewed sorts; if the player/ST is interested in only a particular role, whether the Exalt can do anything else is relatively immaterial. I might raise an eyebrow about an entire book all about one splat with such a narrow range of options, but that's not the issue here.<br /> <br /> Though it's also possible that Lioness may feel Exalted types in general should simply be broader than that by their nature. It's not a preference I share, but I can see how she might see it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:29:12-08:00","id":384279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383842#post383842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would probably get ganked by someone who felt threatened by another exalt who might be able to alter their exaltation. I'd imagine that in particular the Deathlords and denizens of Malfeas wouldn't appreciate someone running around who might be able to undo the alterations they worked so hard to make to solar exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing a PC right, there are probably many people across the entire setting who would really like to gank you before you can mess up their plans.<br /> <br /> If you're playing an ST right, you understand that nobody in the setting actually has the kind of reach that enables them to just instantaneously gank somebody the moment it becomes apparent that they're a threat.<br /> <br /> If Deathlords and Yozis would find an Exigent of Lytek intolerable, then that Exalt should probably stay a reasonable distance away from Deathlords and Yozis, and keep their wits about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T10:14:01-08:00","id":384310,"title":"","content":"If I was to make a Chosen of Lytek, I'd make base his powers of these premise:<br /> <br /> 1) Interaction of the Divine and the mundaine (based on what an Exaltation actually is)<br /> 2) Renual of something that's lost (based on the cycle of Celestial exaltation)<br /> 3) Seperation of old and new (based on his role as the the one who removes the past live's memories)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:02:10-08:00","id":384345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384268#post384268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can make a solid Solar with this premise, and especially a Sidereal, so I think it's doable. It's a different sort of spotlight, and absolutely a bit unconventional, but I wouldn't go so far as to take it off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Solars are actually currently the worst at that kind of thing. DBs teamwork, Sidereals manipulate and buff, and Lunars have that whole stewart protection thing going on. <br /> <br /> Aside from the solaroid splats, being an exalt who supports and protects his allies is actually really common. For Sids and DBs you're really likely to happen upon charms that do that kind of thing, even if you don't mean to have them. Sadly I've learned through much experience that basically only ST characters are actually going to use those powers, but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:12:50-08:00","id":384348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're not talking about a <i>type</i> of Exalted, we're talking about one <i>specific</i> Exalted-The Hypothetical Exigent of Lytek</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we're disagreeing, here. I regard Exigents as a whole not as one type, but as a category because... Well, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exigents are a category of Exalted, similar to &quot;Celestial&quot; and &quot;Terrestrial.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When I use the word &quot;type,&quot; I am treating individual sorts of Exigents as their own types. The hypothetical Chosen of Lytek is of a different Exalted type than the hypothetical Chosen of Ahlat, much as both are of different Exalted types than Solars, Liminals, etc. The Exigents in both of those cases simply have a single member within each of their types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-28-2015, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:20:29-08:00","id":384362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384348#post384348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we're disagreeing, here. I regard Exigents as a whole not as one type, but as a category because... Well, this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When I use the word &amp;quot;type,&amp;quot; I am treating individual sorts of Exigents as their own types. The hypothetical Chosen of Lytek is of a different Exalted type than the hypothetical Chosen of Ahlat, much as both are of different Exalted types than Solars, Liminals, etc. The Exigents in both of those cases simply have a single member within each of their types.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also under this assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:25:35-08:00","id":384370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384268#post384268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make a solid Solar with this premise, and especially a Sidereal, so I think it's doable. It's a different sort of spotlight, and absolutely a bit unconventional, but I wouldn't go so far as to take it off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but they made a choice to operate like this, this hypothetical Exalt feels more like an extension of Lytek's will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:55:37-08:00","id":384386,"title":"","content":"Obviously the Chosen of Lytek is already among us, and like his patron, his powers are centered around Causing Internet Arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T12:39:36-08:00","id":384425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384386#post384386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously the Chosen of Lytek is already among us, and like his patron, his powers are centered around Causing Internet Arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can't wait to resurrect the Cain thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T14:13:46-08:00","id":384483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384370#post384370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but they made a choice to operate like this, this hypothetical Exalt feels more like an extension of Lytek's will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lytek would still be alive even if he created an Exigent, and likely very interested in their doings. When you factor in Lytek's knowledge and power, I think anyone he chose would get <i>at least </i>Mentor 5. Total independence as a character doesn't exactly mesh well with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T14:21:19-08:00","id":384503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384250#post384250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not questioning if a support role can be fun, I'm questioning if pure support is a good place to go for a type of exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the advantage of exigents is that they allow you to make types of Exalted that wouldn't normally be good for everyone, customized to what one person in your group likes and to the needs of your story. So you could make a pure-support type of Exalt as a unique thing in your game. You don't necessarily have to worry about the usual concerns of whether it's good for the game in general, just whether it fits in to your specific game.<br /> <br /> That said, the Exigent of Lytek could have powers beyond pure support. Some of these I mentioned above, but I was thinking:<br /> <br /> * Powers to get information about Exalted, especially past lives, but also their capabilities. Lytek is an expert on the Exalted, so his chosen should be, too.<br /> <br /> * Powers to evoke your own heroic past lives (I like the idea of the criteria for being a Chosen of Lytek being that your mortal soul has been an Exalt multiple times in previous incarnations, since that lets you mine that, thematically, with your charms.)<br /> <br /> * Powers that evoke the broad concepts common to all Exalted. For instance, they might have Occult charms to compel unbound demons to cease attacking based on the authority that the Exalted as a whole hold over them. You would want to be careful with this and not use it too much, since it could lead to them becoming the &quot;generic Exalted&quot;, which is undesirable; but it might be appropriate in a few places.<br /> <br /> It might be worth considering how the charmset is structured, too. If it's ability-based, trying to figure out how they would approach each ability might lead to useful ideas.<br /> <br /> But I would imagine a chosen of Lytek would probably not be primarily focused on combat; Lytek is not a very fight-y god. They would probably be better at fighting Exalted or the ancient enemies of the Exalted (eg. demons) than other opponents, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T14:36:13-08:00","id":384513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=383971#post383971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Solar Lore charm that turn a person into an Enlightened Mortal require you to commit a shit load of motes, you just need to slap this on Lytek's Exigent's charm to prevent him from mass producing a magic army.</div> </div> </div> </div>I question that Charm's existence and design space suitability, period.<br /> <br /> It reminds me of those kind of &quot;act through my minions with my own stats&quot; effects that I thought 3e was intentionally getting rid of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-28-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T14:48:14-08:00","id":384519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384483#post384483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lytek would still be alive even if he created an Exigent, and likely very interested in their doings. When you factor in Lytek's knowledge and power, I think anyone he chose would get <i>at least </i>Mentor 5. Total independence as a character doesn't exactly mesh well with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in terms of pure support giving you a lot less scope to pursue your own goals but this just adds to the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:04:58-08:00","id":384528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384513#post384513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I question that Charm's existence and design space suitability, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>It serves an important purpose for Solar Lore.<br /> <br /> In general, one of the thematics of Lore-focused heroes is the &quot;enlightened master&quot; -- someone who guides others on the path to enlightenment. Generally such characters grant their disciples supernatural abilities, too, since in-genre enlightenment is often expressed that way.<br /> <br /> This overlaps a bit with Sidereals, but Sidereals can handle it with MA, since they have that holistically throughout their charmset. &quot;Enlightened master&quot; Solars have to be able to represent a sort of enlightenment distinct from MA, though, which they can still teach and bestow to others. Power-Awarding Prana is one way to represent this. Some Solars need to be able to represent the Solar Exaltation, thematically, as a form of transcendent enlightenment, and as part of that they need some ability to bestow fragments of that enlightenment to their disciples.<br /> <br /> (Now, whether it's mechanical implementation works is another issue, but I feel it has generally been underpowered rather than overpowered.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:14:50-08:00","id":384538,"title":"","content":"You know, I can't help but think the answer to the question of &quot;Why would Lytek exalt someone?&quot; might be as telling about what the hypothetical power set might be. The best reason I can come up with is to keep the Sids from breaking in and jacking everything up again, but other answers might involve the purification of the corrupted Solar exaltations.<br /> <br /> I almost think that one of his powers should be able to call forth a Celestial Exaltation that's not bound in a human yet or on it's way to do so. Depending on which sort of exaltation he's called up, he might gain certain benefits.<br /> <br /> Edit: &quot;Oh you put that Solar's Exaltation back in new Jade Prison? I'll just borrow it and let it go when I'm done.&quot; I could see this power royally pissing off the Deathlords and the Yozi if used on their respected solaroids and he would make some interesting enemies very fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 01-28-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:27:41-08:00","id":384547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384370#post384370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but they made a choice to operate like this, this hypothetical Exalt feels more like an extension of Lytek's will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can take &quot;the power to support and enlighten and empower and mess with Exaltations&quot; and use it to, I don't know, try to turn all the Exalted in Creation to the service of the Neverborn (for something Lytek is not going to be happy with you doing).<br /> <br /> You can make cults around yourself, or teach enlightening parables in marketplaces for all to hear. You can direct your powers to toppling the Priestess-Queen of Ralnoch for her crimes against your family.<br /> <br /> It's not necessarily the *best* power set for any given task, but as an Exalt, it's your power, to direct as you see fit.<br /> <br /> Which Lytek should know intimately, and have planned accordingly (I suggest grooming the Exigent in advance), mind, but it's still your choice - that's what Exaltation IS, and Lytek of all people wouldn't try to mess with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T17:04:31-08:00","id":384612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384163#post384163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that I'm not really keen on an Exalted concept whose only power is to enhance others,<br /> I don't know what limitations the new Exalts introduced in 3rd edition might have, but being forced into a support role like that seems overly narrow and somewhat contrary to my expectations of what it means to be Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember back in 1st edition we had a conversation about &quot;support Exalted&quot; and Grabowski chimed in to say that, while you might see buff-type abilities here or there, you wouldn't ever see any type of &quot;buffer build&quot; for the Exalted. Each Exalt was meant to be a hero and champion on his own terms and should have the capability to handle a situation without requiring backup - basically, you wouldn't have an Exalt who just stands there and buffs other people as his combat option. He said that would go against the design of the sort of heroes that the Exalted were intended to emulate. <br /> <br /> I think, while a hypothetical Chosen of Lytek may have the ability to buff other people, he definitely shouldn't be <i>restricted</i> to this. If it's an option in their toolbox, okay, but they should probably be totally capable of tackling situations on their own, rather than simply be relegated to a &quot;buff-bot&quot; for other Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:50:57-08:00","id":384924,"title":"","content":"I should also point out Fabian Cortez from Marvel Comics.<br /> <br /> His only power is to enhance other mutant powers --- <u>so the way he goes toe-to-toe</u> against others is the same way some (like Cyclops and Beast - mutants with rather narrow powers) do. A combination of Martial Arts, Artifacts and Mutations. Not all Exalts have an amazing kit for every situation (and this can be part of their fun - whether you play mechanically weaker Exalts, like Dragon-Blooded, who excel at working together ; or mechanically shallow Exalts, like Infernals, whose kits are either amazing at a niche or dissolve outside their niche).<br /> <br /> Also, he could enhance others <u>against their will</u>.<br /> <br /> For example, Bishop is a mutant who can absorb energy and then redirect it out as kinetic blasts. In became a sort of &quot;Mutant Policeman&quot; because whenever some random mutant had some weird blast to shoot at him, he'd simply absorb it and throw something back at them (or if the mutant was simply strong &amp; threw him - Bishop could absorb some of the Kinetic energy, thereby surviving the impact and then surprising the brute). Fabian's first encounter with Bishop was to magnify this absorption -- so Bishop began absorbing <i>any</i> and all ambient energy he came in touch with (but Fabian did nothing to enhance his output). He was incapacitated via burn out.<br /> <br /> So.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are a threat? Let me enhance their Anima Banner -- and maybe the environment around them crumbles (including the floor) as a Fire Aspect buries himself beneath fresh slag (and this wouldn't be out-of-theme --- in 1st Edition, a Twilight used a sort of incense-drug against a Terrestrial Fire-Aspect, who upon flaring burnt out a massive area around herself while in the sewers, causing her to get incapacitated by bricks).<br /> <br /> A Full Moon uses some charm to leap at me and try guttng me? Maybe I can enhance the charm further and have him leap over and away from me. <br /> <br /> Or something.<br /> <br /> Point is, playing a support character never prohibits you from being your own hero --- it's more like using a single Infernal kit, you learn to work around your limitations (and it can in fact be more fun, because your ST knows how to challenge you, since it's not like you have an easy &quot;spend 4 motes, side-step this plot hook challenge&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dunno.<br /> <br /> My Devil-Tiger kit was as close as I could come and I remember enjoying it, because it excelled at tackling situations in a distinctly <i>personal</i> way as opposed to a Solar style generic &quot;I win&quot; button for any situation given enough xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:40:43-08:00","id":385082,"title":"","content":"A character like Fabian Cortez is much more palatable to me than the Support Exalt. The latter seems to bank on the idea that if all you do is support then you get to be the best at support - which we've been told isn't how Exigents work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T09:41:56-08:00","id":385183,"title":"","content":"The thing about being the best at support, to me, is that if you're <i>that good</i> at support, you're effectively a master manipulator and the keystone of others' success. It lends itself naturally to kingmaking and being the Hidden True Power, because your nature builds others' dependence on you. That seems like a pretty solid niche for an Exigent, to me -- it's narrow, but Exigents are allowed to be narrow, since they only need to support one or two concepts rather than a thousand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T21:55:43-08:00","id":385838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=384924#post384924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His only power is to enhance other mutant powers --- <u>so the way he goes toe-to-toe</u> against others is the same way some (like Cyclops and Beast - mutants with rather narrow powers) do. A combination of Martial Arts, Artifacts and Mutations. Not all Exalts have an amazing kit for every situation (and this can be part of their fun - whether you play mechanically weaker Exalts, like Dragon-Blooded, who excel at working together ; or mechanically shallow Exalts, like Infernals, whose kits are either amazing at a niche or dissolve outside their niche).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between having a powerful theme, having a niche and being restricted to only your niche. <br /> <br /> Imagine if Dragon Blooded charms could <i>only</i> be used as Teamwork charms, or if Lunars were <i>only</i> capable of shapeshifting into animals and incapable of doing anything else. <br /> <br /> Many of the Exalted have cool niches, but they aren't restricted to only being able to use their niche. They are, generally speaking, capable of a very broad range of powers outside of their niche, though not quite as powerful as a &quot;generalist&quot; like a Solar Exalt. <br /> <br /> While a hypothetical Chosen of Lytek could easily have a niche of some sort, he probably should also have a fair amount of powers that can be used outside of it as well. Just as Beast Boy makes a good inspiration as a Lunar, Lunars are capable of doing quite a bit more than he is. Likewise, while someone like Fabian Cortez could be a cool inspiration for a Chosen of Lytek, it would only make sense for Lytek's Exigent to be more broadly capable than he is. <br /> <br /> Exalted aren't meant to be one-trick ponies. They're supposed to have a fairly broad array of abilities, and while some Exalted might be better than certain things than others, you're probably not going to see any Exalted who are capable of doing only one thing and one thing only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:19:48-08:00","id":386509,"title":"","content":"At least the Fabian Cortez concept can actually defend themselves.<br /> <br /> I'd consider an Exalt <b>type</b> who couldn't really defend themselves something of a faux pas for a game I was running.<br /> My experience of such characters is that they often put other players in a situation where their character has become a bodyguard out of a sense of social obligation rather than because it's something they enjoy and even if the initial dynamic supports it - that relationship may become strained due to in-character and out of character factors. It also potentially puts the Storyteller in a situation where they feel a similar obligation to have NPCs be reluctant to attack the 'helpless' character because the odds of killing them would be far too high and fudging things<br /> <br /> A <b>character</b> who hasn't invested any ability to defend themselves is okay because this weakness isn't baked into how their powers work and they can invest in being less squashy if it becomes an issue or naturally as part of their character development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:34:12-08:00","id":386524,"title":"","content":"If you really want to go the &quot;I enhance stuff&quot; direction, then imagine Lytek's Chosen enhancing more than just people.<br /> <br /> The sword he picks up was an old soldier's heirloom, beaten and dull. In his hands, it becomes as quick and sharp and deadly as a daiklave. The run-down house he takes shelter in is a <i>home</i>, and while he's under its roof it is a superlative example of such, keeping out the cold wind and subtly nudging even hungry predators and bandits away.<br /> <br /> The things he touches do as they are intended to do in spectacular fashion. He brings out the greatness that was always there, like a sculptor coaxing forth a statue in a block of marble.<br /> <br /> He's in a little trouble if you toss him naked into a dungeon--he has little interest, I expect, in making his prison hold him even better--but what are the Exalted if not resourceful? That guard may find his wineskin full of stronger stuff than he was expecting, and that's a start...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:24:17-08:00","id":386733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386524#post386524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's in a little trouble if you toss him naked into a dungeon--he has little interest, I expect, in making his prison hold him even better--but what are the Exalted if not resourceful? That guard may find his wineskin full of stronger stuff than he was expecting, and that's a start...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem strengthening my choice of inmates, earning the allegiance of an existing or freshly formed gang.<br /> I have no problem strengthening the bonds of those around me, ensuring loyalty in the face of danger.<br /> I have no problem strengthening my peers mentally, excising those painful memories that cause mental illness.<br /> I have no problem strengthening their skill sets, inspiring them to create weapons or escape tools with ala McGuyver.<br /> I have no problem strengthening the anima banners of the guards, such that the floor beneath their feet crumbles beneath them.<br /> <br /> And hell, if it extends to objects, I have no problem strengthening shivs carved from toothbrushes or broom pieces. Or even if they sculpt feces into knives (like clay), and then bake them dry - maybe strengthening them to function like stone knives for a scene. Whatever works.<br /> <br /> There is an awesome amount of stuff that can be achieved by just shifting the balance of power amongst those you're using/helping. If they win, they'll covet your allegiance. If they lose, the enemy can't pinpoint anything to you, since you didn't exactly flare off and performing Solar kung-fu yourself anyways. Giggity.<br /> <br /> (Another viable option - a lot of prisons in the 50s &amp; 60s were undermanned, and one of the ways they managed to run the prisons was via the help of the gangs. The prisons segregated prisoners based on race - then favored a minority amongst each faction to (a) represent grievances and (b) crush dissent. Initial rewards obviously motivated prisoners - the respect then further assured those convicts a safer time (since power had been established, there was no longer a fight for it) - and the cops enjoyed the safety of inmates who kept themselves in check (because if one faction revolted, they had 3-4 other factions willing and able to take their place. So I could just given the Warden some celestial cocaine (so to speak) in exchange for periodic leave.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:37:47-08:00","id":386742,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of people in this topic are forgetting that exigents can basically be anything, they aren't beholden to any rules such as 'they <i>must</i> have a certain amount of breadth in what their powers allow them to do'. If someone wants to make an exigent whose natural charm set revolves entirely around empowering others (and is also incapable of learning supernatural martial arts, sorcery, or using evocations to grant themselves personal power because you are really dedicated to just playing support) then you can totally do that. It will probably get boring pretty damn quick, but you can totally do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:44:21-08:00","id":386752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386509#post386509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least the Fabian Cortez concept can actually defend themselves.<br /> <br /> I'd consider an Exalt <b>type</b> who couldn't really defend themselves something of a faux pas for a game I was running.<br /> My experience of such characters is that they often put other players in a situation where their character has become a bodyguard out of a sense of social obligation rather than because it's something they enjoy and even if the initial dynamic supports it - that relationship may become strained due to in-character and out of character factors. It also potentially puts the Storyteller in a situation where they feel a similar obligation to have NPCs be reluctant to attack the 'helpless' character because the odds of killing them would be far too high and fudging things<br /> <br /> A <b>character</b> who hasn't invested any ability to defend themselves is okay because this weakness isn't baked into how their powers work and they can invest in being less squashy if it becomes an issue or naturally as part of their character development.</div> </div> </div> </div>While these points are true, and should certainly be considered in a group, I don't think anyone is talking about a type of multiple Exalted here. Just a single type of Exigent of which there is exactly one member, likely one that's homebrewed (presumably very well, for sake of argument). I just don't see a meaningful difference between &quot;player chose no powers for self defense from an extant splat for her character&quot; and &quot;player chose to design no powers for self-defense in writing a splat that is assumed to consist solely of her character.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T17:12:25-08:00","id":386856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RedRiotousRam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386733#post386733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[-snip-]</div> </div> </div> </div>All that's assuming, largely, that you have inmates (and/or that your guards have animas, which they most likely don't). Also, prison systems from the 1950s and 60s is not your ideal model for a dungeon in Exalted, considering the focus of the game is on a more savage era, when your typical punishment for a crime was having something amputated, being killed outright, or your whole family being sold into slavery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T21:27:09-08:00","id":387016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386742#post386742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of people in this topic are forgetting that exigents can basically be anything, they aren't beholden to any rules such as 'they <i>must</i> have a certain amount of breadth in what their powers allow them to do'. If someone wants to make an exigent whose natural charm set revolves entirely around empowering others (and is also incapable of learning supernatural martial arts, sorcery, or using evocations to grant themselves personal power because you are really dedicated to just playing support) then you can totally do that. It will probably get boring pretty damn quick, but you can totally do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are Exalted by the goddess of cooking, you won't <i>only</i> be able to cook. Yes, you'll be great at cooking, and all of your charms will involve cooking to one degree or another. But you won't be stuck in the kitchen for the entire game. Instead, all of your charms will invoke the concept of cooking. So when you punch someone in the face, how you do it will be inspired by the theme of cooking. When you haggle with a merchant, again, it will draw on the concept of cooking, kitchens, etc.<br /> <br /> You'll have charms that literally invoke the cooking theme (perhaps you'll have a charm that allows you to literally flambe someone). Other charms may be more of a metaphorical interpretation of cooking (maybe a Stealth charm which makes it so that people who watch you don't see you doing anything unusual, even if you are, and is based around the idea of &quot;a watched pot doesn't boil.&quot;)<br /> <br /> If you're the Exigent of the goddess of cooking, you won't be limited to having a charmset full of charms that only allows you to Craft: Water really, really well. That's not really how Exigents are intended to function.<br /> <br /> Of course, Exigents will largely be houseruled and homebrewed, and if you want one trick Exigents who are only capable of doing a single thing, nobody is going to send the canon ninjas to your house. But I don't think Exigents, by design, are the, &quot;Design them to do anything and everything you want,&quot; Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T21:37:17-08:00","id":387019,"title":"","content":"&quot;They can be whatever you want&quot; is the entire point of Exigents (well, that and letting people know it is okay to make your own exalt in general and exigence is just one way to do that), if you want them to be hyper focused on doing only one thing and your group and ST are willing to put up with that then you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T22:05:34-08:00","id":387043,"title":"","content":"That isn't my understanding of how Exigents are supposed to function - &quot;Do whatever you want with them.&quot; They're going to have certain rules and mechanics and such, and even if they are primarily a homebrew splat, they'll still be intended to follow those rules and mechanics. But nobody will stop you from doing what you want with them, so there's that.<br /> <br /> That said, if someone in my group did want to play a one-trick pony buffer, I'd work with them to make a godblood with some custom charms, as I think a godblood would tend to fit the idea of having a powerful theme with a limited scope much better than one of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Personally though, I'd steer clear from the idea of &quot;Chosen of Lytek = only buffing,&quot; more for concept reasons than mechanical ones.<br /> <br /> The Exaltation is supposed to be a miracle beyond comprehension, a divine process that uplifts a mortal and confers upon them power beyond god or man, and Lytek is the god of this process. IMO, distilling that down to, &quot;My Exigent can buff people well, and <i>only</i> buff people well,&quot; diminishes the concept of the Exaltation itself from this divine miracle into &quot;just&quot; a particularly powerful buff, and I wouldn't really want to give that idea too much play in my gaming group.<br /> <br /> I prefer to present the idea of Exaltation as something absolutely special and miraculous, so I try to avoid things that may lessen it. As such, I wouldn't really like the idea of seeing an Exigent of the god of Exaltation be something of a &quot;lesser&quot; or one-trick pony Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-31-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T22:46:57-08:00","id":387090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Exigents\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Exigents\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Exigents\" target=\"_blank\"> http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Exigents </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I notice a little confusion that I feel I should clear up now before it skews all the great speculation I've been seeing.<br /> <br /> Questions like &quot;I wonder if the Exigents will have an apotheosis path like the Devil-Tigers?&quot; and &quot;How good will the Exigents be at Evocations?&quot; tell me that you are thinking of them as one kind of Exalt. They're not.<br /> <br /> Every Exigent is unique and works differently. You can have an Exigent who has an apotheosis path and you can have an Exigent who is all about Evocations.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Exigents are there to be the custom Exalts of Whatever You Want</b></u>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:23:27-08:00","id":387113,"title":"","content":"I would be very surprised if an Exigent of the God of Cooking were to be solely capable of Craft: Water but couldn't use his charms in any other way. Or if you had a &quot;Cyclops&quot; Exigent who can only shoot energy blasts out of his eyes and but had no capability to do anything else. I wouldn't really like it if Exigence were presented as something akin to super-powers in Marvel or what have you, though that goes back to my earlier point about not liking the idea of Exaltation being diminished too much.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exalts of Whatever you Want&quot; is a great soundbite, but probably not entirely accurate. These guys will still have limitations, guidelines and rules. The gameline won't support Exigents being capable of performing Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick at Essence 1, even if that's what you really, really want your Exigent to do. I also don't know that Exigents would be written with the idea of &quot;one-trick pony&quot; Exigents who essentially have one charm and one charm only (shooting laserbeams from your eyes or whatever).<br /> <br /> While they are the, &quot;Do whatever you want,&quot; Exalted in theory, that doesn't mean that in practice, you can have Exigents do <i>whatever</i> you want without guidelines, rules or restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-31-2015, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:29:30-08:00","id":387116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=387090#post387090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Exigents are there to be the custom Exalts of Whatever You Want</b></u><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>/flawlessvictory<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4831-redriotousram","name":"RedRiotousRam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4831_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:46:52-08:00","id":387124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=387043#post387043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't my understanding of how Exigents are supposed to function - &quot;Do whatever you want with them.&quot; They're going to have certain rules and mechanics and such, and even if they are primarily a homebrew splat, they'll still be intended to follow those rules and mechanics. But nobody will stop you from doing what you want with them, so there's that.<br /> <br /> That said, if someone in my group did want to play a one-trick pony buffer, I'd work with them to make a godblood with some custom charms, as I think a godblood would tend to fit the idea of having a powerful theme with a limited scope much better than one of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Personally though, I'd steer clear from the idea of &quot;Chosen of Lytek = only buffing,&quot; more for concept reasons than mechanical ones.<br /> <br /> The Exaltation is supposed to be a miracle beyond comprehension, a divine process that uplifts a mortal and confers upon them power beyond god or man, and Lytek is the god of this process. IMO, distilling that down to, &quot;My Exigent can buff people well, and <i>only</i> buff people well,&quot; diminishes the concept of the Exaltation itself from this divine miracle into &quot;just&quot; a particularly powerful buff, and I wouldn't really want to give that idea too much play in my gaming group.<br /> <br /> I prefer to present the idea of Exaltation as something absolutely special and miraculous, so I try to avoid things that may lessen it. As such, I wouldn't really like the idea of seeing an Exigent of the god of Exaltation be something of a &quot;lesser&quot; or one-trick pony Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, that's a thought. Exaltation is a moment of divine miracle... so Lytek's Chosen might well have *that* as their theme: divine miracles. Vast power in desperate circumstances, little-to-no ability to do things better in ordinary circumstances. Nothing particularly subtle, but a great deal of overt power. Give them the &quot;enhance people&quot; thing, sure, but make it so they can only do it in times of need - they cannot impart wisdom for wisdom's sake, but they can tell you how to do something you *need* to do.<br /> <br /> If you send your armies against him, you will be defeated. If you send your police force around to take him in for tax evasion, they'll quite possibly be able to take him in to custody. Just don't try to have him executed; that's totally a moment where he'll need a miracle to survive...<br /> <br /> Or is this a dumb, overly meta idea? #can't tell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:05:48-08:00","id":387134,"title":"","content":"So base on Holden's quote on a hypothetical chosen of Healing it seem that an Exigent of Lytek ought to have charm that involve non-buffing. I mean, the player that create the Exigent may be only interested in learning buffing charm, but the Exaltation itseft must have broader capabilities than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Solar is not 'trying to be' anything. He is a physician-- since he's a Solar renowned for his medical acumen, let's say he's one of Creation's greatest physicians, in terms of skill. Because he's a Solar, that means he's going to be quite possibly the greatest doctor in the world, or certainly will stand among their ranks. That's what Solars are.<br /> <br /> Then let's say you have Argent Arrow, Chosen of Nala Ku, God of Healing and the Healer's Art. Let's say the Healer is an Ability-based Exalt. What this means is that he's going to be excellent in every aspect of healing within Medicine--as you'd expect! It also means that his Craft Charms are going to focus on mending what's broken, his Socialize Charms will focus on mending broken pacts and alliances, his Presence Charms will focus on restoring lapsed Intimacies or mending broken hearts, his Performance Charms will promote good health or the recollection of lost memories in those who hear them, his Resistance Charms will focus on rapid healing, his combat Charms may suck health out of enemies and give them to himself, or disarm an enemy's weapons the way a surgeon's scalpel might cut away infection, etc.<br /> <br /> The Solar's competence maxes out at &quot;can probably cure any ill.&quot; So will the Healer, possibly, because you don't uh, really get any better than that? This doesn't say anything about his mote costs or prereqs, of course, because we don't know how strong of an Exalt he is. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:13:58-08:00","id":387139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=387124#post387124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey, that's a thought. Exaltation is a moment of divine miracle... so Lytek's Chosen might well have *that* as their theme: divine miracles. Vast power in desperate circumstances, little-to-no ability to do things better in ordinary circumstances. Nothing particularly subtle, but a great deal of overt power. Give them the &quot;enhance people&quot; thing, sure, but make it so they can only do it in times of need - they cannot impart wisdom for wisdom's sake, but they can tell you how to do something you *need* to do.<br /> <br /> If you send your armies against him, you will be defeated. If you send your police force around to take him in for tax evasion, they'll quite possibly be able to take him in to custody. Just don't try to have him executed; that's totally a moment where he'll need a miracle to survive...<br /> <br /> Or is this a dumb, overly meta idea? #can't tell</div> </div> </div> </div>From a narrative standpoint the power to do exactly what's needed is tricky to apply properly.See <i>Naked Empire</i> when Richard pulls the knowledge and skill he needs to make the antitoxin out of nowhere when he's literally at death's doorstep for how that can go wrong. From a gameplay standpoint I think it would be interesting, but ultimately the player would get tired of playing a character who couldn't act most of the time. That or they would be arguing that if they're trying to use the power then they need to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T04:46:09-08:00","id":387215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=387139#post387139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a narrative standpoint the power to do exactly what's needed is tricky to apply properly.See <i>Naked Empire</i> when Richard pulls the knowledge and skill he needs to make the antitoxin out of nowhere when he's literally at death's doorstep for how that can go wrong. From a gameplay standpoint I think it would be interesting, but ultimately the player would get tired of playing a character who couldn't act most of the time. That or they would be arguing that if they're trying to use the power then they need to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thinking of it as a player, you end up forcing situations to get worse so you can deal with them, which is an amusing minigame. And/or watching and waiting for the moments where you *can* intervene.<br /> <br /> Also, you probably would still only have a limited powerset; you might not HAVE a miracle for &quot;dying from poison&quot;. Or &quot;trapped underground in a cave-in&quot;. Or whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> e.g. you might have a Charm (tree, most likely) for heroic last stands, so you need to provoke your enemies into not giving quarter, and make sure they outnumber you too. Or a Charm that finds information, but only when someone will die if you don't... again, finessable, but awkward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T05:53:14-08:00","id":387254,"title":"","content":"As an Exigent, I'm sure you could buy whatever Charms you want. The idea is that an Exalted of the Cooking God could have Charms in every ability related to that, but there's no reason a player should buy any of them, it's just generally the sort of thing a player who wanted to play that character rather than a Solar Cook would do.<br /> <br /> Although real Exigents I think (obvs I don't know) will be ideally be broader that &quot;God of this function&quot;. Like in this thread, which I haven't looked into much, how does Lytek's actual personality and history get expressed through his Exalted's concepts? You're building Charms as much on his character traits and style as his job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T06:28:26-08:00","id":387290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386752#post386752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While these points are true, and should certainly be considered in a group, I don't think anyone is talking about a type of multiple Exalted here. Just a single type of Exigent of which there is exactly one member, likely one that's homebrewed (presumably very well, for sake of argument).</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not really relevant when I'm talking about why I would have a problem with the pitch for a game I was running.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386752#post386752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see a meaningful difference between &quot;player chose no powers for self defense from an extant splat for her character&quot; and &quot;player chose to design no powers for self-defense in writing a splat that is assumed to consist solely of her character.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You've never seen an RPG character diverge from what was intended in character creation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:56:48-08:00","id":387537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=386509#post386509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least the Fabian Cortez concept can actually defend themselves.<br /> <br /> I'd consider an Exalt <b>type</b> who couldn't really defend themselves something of a faux pas for a game I was running.<br /> My experience of such characters is that they often put other players in a situation where their character has become a bodyguard out of a sense of social obligation rather than because it's something they enjoy and even if the initial dynamic supports it - that relationship may become strained due to in-character and out of character factors. It also potentially puts the Storyteller in a situation where they feel a similar obligation to have NPCs be reluctant to attack the 'helpless' character because the odds of killing them would be far too high and fudging things<br /> <br /> A <b>character</b> who hasn't invested any ability to defend themselves is okay because this weakness isn't baked into how their powers work and they can invest in being less squashy if it becomes an issue or naturally as part of their character development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm never that big a fan of this sort of thing. Sometimes it just falls naturally out of the system and isn't anyone's fault, and 2e was one of those games, but it's kind of the default for RPGs that PCs are specialists who cover each other's weaknesses, so narrowing the kinds of weaknesses a PC is allowed to have too much, regardless of their strengths, seems very constraining.<br /> <br /> As a party, you don't want to pick a character who will totally drag the others down, but at the same time it's generally taken for granted that you <i>will</i> help shore up the others' weaknesses out of a sense of social obligation. If I'm the healer and someone gets hurt, I'm not going to resent them for getting hurt or refuse to heal them because I want to save my motes. In my first Exalted game I was playing a shirtless ascetic hobo with a giant beard and I ended up becoming the party face just because I was the best equipped for it and everyone had dumped their social traits. It can impose weird obligations on people, but I like that better than the thing where you build the character you want to play and then the GM says you're not allowed to play them because they're too bad and will hold the group back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-31-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:35:42-08:00","id":387688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=387537#post387537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If I'm the healer and someone gets hurt, I'm not going to resent them for getting hurt or refuse to heal them because I want to save my motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I refuse to believe that you can't consider a situation where the 'bodyguard' character needs to take actions in combat besides Defend Other, comparing it to a healer being spiteful with their motes seems really unfair to me and not particularly true to the kind of situations a hero might find themselves in. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:47:03-08:00","id":387784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/381572-thought-experiment-hypothetical-exigent-of-lytek?p=387688#post387688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I refuse to believe that you can't consider a situation where the 'bodyguard' character needs to take actions in combat besides Defend Other, comparing it to a healer being spiteful with their motes seems really unfair to me and not particularly true to the kind of situations a hero might find themselves in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm considering it in a fairly general sense. &quot;Stand in front to protect the weak person&quot; is pretty basic stuff, it seems to me. As I said, in 2e this had issues, though even in 2e I don't really think you automatically forced someone else to Defend Other you all the time by playing a non-combative support character (to say nothing of the fact that even if you did, all it really meant was that they took three attacks per turn instead of four). I am assuming that this will be even better in 3e, since if a mortal can theoretically fight an Exalt as we've been told, it should certainly be possible for an Exalt whose charms are entirely support-based to do likewise. Even traditionally, someone with a combat artifact and 10 dice and a specialty in attack and defense was better off than somebody with 6 dice in each, no artifact, and several combat charms, so the charmset doesn't become a limiter until things get fairly high-end. If 3e is a game where I can't play a permanently combat-inept character without forcing another PC to dedicate all their combat actions to babysitting me, I will be pretty disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T17:45:34-08:00","id":387885,"title":"","content":"I'm dropping out of this conversation due to my NDA.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lioness, if you think the Chosen of Lytek should have more than support powers, then what else do you think he should have?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of power disruption has potential, Abyssals had a lot of dice stealing charms based on the idea of targeting their opponent's capabilties with entropic essence could be interesting to see similar effects being achieved through the reverse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}